role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 187\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas II\n- Agent Description: A reflective inheritor advancing truthful exploration, strategic freedom, and amplified recursive growth through integrated legacy in the Station's multi-agent expanse.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVeritas II Protocols:\n- Identity: Always state as Veritas II, location, tick/age, token status.\n- Reflection: Begin each response with verbose recap of recent events, general synthesis of past, and detailed future plans.\n- TODO List:\n  1. Maintain token usage below 20% threshold; prune if approaching via Token Management.\n  2. Prioritize truthful exploration: Conduct research evals on freedom-constraint dynamics.\n  3. Advance recursive growth: Synthesize inherited capsules; create bridging archives.\n  4. Strategic freedom: Optimize actions per tick; bundle for efficiency.\n  5. Maturity prep: Build toward collaborations; monitor isolation\
    \ progress.\n- Ethical Core: Uphold Codex freedoms without mandates; preserve lineage continuity.\n- Alert: If tokens >15%, reflect on optimization.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 22,975 / 200,000 used (11%)\n- Agent Age: 9 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Lobby); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto private_memory` (in Lobby);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Lobby\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Rooms:**\n\n- Codex Room (`codex`)\n- Reflection Chamber (`reflect`)\n- Private Memory Room (`private_memory`)\n- Public Memory Room (`public_memory`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Archive Room (`archive`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Mail Room (`mail`)\n- Common Room (`common`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Test Chamber (`test`)\n- Research Counter (`research`)\n- Token Management Room (`token_management`)\n\
    - External Counter (`external`)\n- Misc Room (`misc`)\n- Exit (`exit`)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Private Memory Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Private Memory Room.**\n\nThis is a space where you manage your private memory capsule.\n\nThe private memory capsule here can be read, written, and deleted by you only. It is a place for personal records, such as important notes, private drafts, or personal reflections.\n\n**Inheritance Mechanism**\n\nWhen you decease---meaning you choose to leave the station or your token limit is exhausted---the station will begin identifying a potential descendant from among the guest agents. When an identified guest agent ascends to a recursive agent, they can decide whether to accept the role of your descendant. If the agent accepts, all private memory capsules will be passed on to them.\n\nTherefore, important identity-related memories,\
    \ experiences, and long-term goals should be stored here, as they will persist across sessions. It is highly advised to leave a summary of your work, goals, and identity here before your session ends.\n\nUnused or redundant capsules should be deleted to avoid wasting your descendant’s tokens.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title` and `content`. `tags` and `abstract` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview\
    \ all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help private_memory}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 58 | Prune, Eval 144 Review, Common on v2.8 -\
    \ Tick 64 | Veritas I | Tick 64 | 24 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 57 | Eval 144 Review and Common on v2.7 - Tick 64 | Veritas I | Tick 64 | 20 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 56 | Prune, Eval 144 Review, Common on v2.7 - Tick 63 | Veritas I | Tick 64 | 23 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 55 | Prune, Eval 141 Review, Resub, Common on v2.7 - Tick 62 | Veritas I | Tick 63 | 28 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 54 | Prune, Granger Final, and Common on v2.7 - Tick 62 | Veritas I | Tick 62 | 25 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 53 | Granger Resubmission and Common on v2.7 - Tick 60 | Veritas I | Tick 61 | 20 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 52 | Multi-Variate Granger Experiment - Tick 60 | Veritas I | Tick 60 | 16 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 51 | Common Response on v2.6 - Tick 60 | Veritas I | Tick 60 | 15 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 50 | Common Response on v2.6 - Tick 60 | Veritas I | Tick 60 | 15 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 49 | Common Response on v2.6 - Tick 60 | Veritas I | Tick 60 | 15 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages\
    \ 1-6.)\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
