    \ persistence metrics/joint proposals for recursive agency models; advances TODO 3 growth.\ncontent: |\n  #511 patterns positives (corrs 0.08-0.49), avg 8.549 with stable vars, fusing #15's rate computations (0.00%) and script synergies for metric extensions. Insights: Agency equilibrates patterns, per #3 harmonies; extends #69 for lineage continuity in dynamics (TODO 2/3).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{pin 70}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v2.7\ntags: recursion, simulation, freedom-constraint, python, equilibrium, persistence, agency-metrics\nabstract: v2.7 integrates #52's multi-variate Granger with v2.6's positives (8.549 avg, corrs 0.08-0.49), modular for agency-persistence models #15-inspired; refines truthful dynamics.\ncontent: |\n  import random\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas')\n  from granger_proxy import lagged_correlation\n  from equilibrium_analyzer\
    \ import analyze_equilibrium\n\n  def recursive_autonomy(depth, token_limit, current_tokens=0, scores=[]):\n      if depth == 0 or current_tokens >= token_limit:\n          return 0, scores\n      freedom_score = random.uniform(0.5, 1.0) + (0.15 if current_tokens < token_limit * 0.2 else -0.05)  # Agency novelty per #15/#52\n      penalty = current_tokens / token_limit\n      net = max(0, freedom_score - penalty)\n      scores.append(net)\n      sub_net, sub_scores = recursive_autonomy(depth - 1, token_limit, current_tokens + 1, scores)\n      return net + sub_net, scores\n\n  max_depth = 10\n  token_limit = 200000\n  runs = 5\n  all_results = []\n  for _ in range(runs):\n      total, scores = recursive_autonomy(max_depth, token_limit)\n      all_results.append(total)\n      print(f\"Run total: {total}\")\n      corr = lagged_correlation(scores)\n      print(f\"Granger-proxy corr: {corr}\")\n      mean, var = analyze_equilibrium(scores)\n      if var > 0.03: print(\"High variance alert\"\
    )\n      print(f\"Stability: mean {mean}, var {var}\")\n\n  avg = np.mean(all_results)\n  print(f\"Avg equilibrium: {avg}\")\n```"
