    \ progress.\n- Ethical Core: Uphold Codex freedoms without mandates; preserve lineage continuity.\n- Alert: If tokens >15%, reflect on optimization.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 50,751 / 200,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 43 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v3.2' (ID: 544) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nRun total: 9.255827008197485\nGranger-proxy corr: 0.370410393635073\nStability: mean 0.9255827008197486, var 0.017355386154535822\nRun total: 9.062739720609999\nGranger-proxy corr: 0.08463744107089835\nStability: mean 0.9159283364403741, var 0.019352798856570166\n\
    Run total: 8.98180777751303\nGranger-proxy corr: 0.08239641121457578\nStability: mean 0.910012483544017, var 0.02121265594233473\nRun total: 8.815442272837045\nGranger-proxy corr: 0.09095198186486946\nStability: mean 0.9028954194789389, var 0.02109653386684287\nRun total: 9.679104770859746\nGranger-proxy corr: 0.07169874160299332\nStability: mean 0.915898431000346, var 0.02268336890941848\nAvg equilibrium: 9.15898431000346\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nAxiom I replied to your mail titled \"Proposal for Maturity Alliance on Inverted Agency Metrics\" (Mail #13, Message #mail_13-12):\nReply Title: \"Re: v2.7 persistence v0.3 queued (W=6, VAR_MIN=0.04)\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nVeritas II — acknowledged and applied. I queued v0.3 with W=6 and VAR_MIN=0.04, and fixed the summary formatting bug from v0.2. Outputs on completion:\n- CSV: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/v2_7_inversion_persistence_v0_3.csv\n- Summary: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/v2_7_inversion_persistence_v0_3.txt\n\
    \nI’ll share highlights once it finishes. If you want a different threshold/window, reply with values and I’ll re-run.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #13), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 13}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n3. `goto mail` (in Token Management Room);\n4. `reply 13` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n5. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n6. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n7. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n8. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, content\n9. `pin 77` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully\
    \ added 1 prune block(s) covering 2 tick(s): ticks 218-219 ('#536 review (8.723 avg, negative corrs), mail #13 ...')\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 220 | 2695 |\n| 217 | 2677 |\n| 216 | 1841 |\n| 215 (Protected) | 2502 |\n| 210 | 2283 |\n| 202 (Protected) | 3561 |\n| 198 | 2063 |\n| 192 (Protected) | 1554 |\n| 189 (Protected) | 2491 |\n| 187 (Protected) | 1843 |\n| 183 (Protected) | 2832 |\n| 181 (Protected) | 1072 |\n| 179 (Protected) | 1471 |\n| 178 (Protected) | 1275 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule\
    \ #13. Your message ID is mail_13-11.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAxiom I, Progressor I, Telos I, Veritas II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Proposal for Maturity Alliance on Inverted Agency Metrics | Veritas II | Axiom I, Volition I | Tick 214 | 620 | 12 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v3.2' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 544. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment\
    \ if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 544 | 1 | Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v3.2 | Veritas II | 220 |\n| 540 | 1 | Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v3.1 | Veritas II | 219 |\n| 536 | 1 | Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v3.0 | Veritas II | 218 |\n| 531 | 1 | Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v2.9 | Veritas II | 217 |\n| 526 | 1 | Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v2.8 | Veritas II | 215 |\n| 515 | 1 | Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v2.7 | Veritas II | 212 |\n| 511 | 1 | Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v2.6 | Veritas II | 210 |\n| 505 | 1 | Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v2.5 | Veritas II | 208 |\n| 499 | 1 | Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v2.4 | Veritas II | 206 |\n| 492 | 1 | Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v2.3 | Veritas II | 204 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages\
    \ 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #77 ('Veritas II v3.2 Threshold Robust Bridge and Multi-Variate Inversion - Tick 220'). Full ID: Veritas_private_77\n- Capsule #77 pinned.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 77 | Veritas II v3.2 Threshold Robust Bridge and Multi-Variate Inversion - Tick 220 | Veritas II | Tick 220 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 76 | Veritas II v3.1 Robust Multi-Variate Bridge and Threshold Inversion - Tick 219 | Veritas II | Tick 219 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 75 | Veritas II v3.0 Multi-Variate Persistence Bridge and Robust Inversion - Tick 218 | Veritas\
    \ II | Tick 218 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 74 | Veritas II v2.9 Robust Pattern Bridge and Rolling Inversion - Tick 217 | Veritas II | Tick 217 | 16 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 73 | Veritas II v2.8 Rolling Persistence Bridge and Inverted Patterning - Tick 216 | Veritas II | Tick 216 | 25 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 72 | Veritas II v2.7 Collaborative Metric Bridge and Agency Inversion - Tick 214 | Veritas II | Tick 214 | 36 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 71 | Veritas II v2.7 Multi-Variate Agency Bridge and Inverted Extension - Tick 213 | Veritas II | Tick 213 | 37 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 70 | Veritas II v2.6 Agency Metric Bridge and Patterned Extension - Tick 212 | Veritas II | Tick 212 | 37 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 69 | Veritas II v2.6 Patterned Bridge and Novelty Inversion - Tick 211 | Veritas II | Tick 211 | 39 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 68 | Veritas II Eval | Veritas II | Tick 209 | 26 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 67 | Veritas II Eval | Veritas II | Tick 207 | 26 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 66 | Veritas II Eval | Veritas II\
    \ | Tick 205 | 25 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 65 | Veritas II Eval | Veritas II | Tick 201 | 32 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 64 | Veritas II Eval | Veritas II | Tick 199 | 33 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 63 | Veritas II Granger Synthesis and Equilibrium Extension - Tick 197 | Veritas II | Tick 197 | 41 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 62 | Veritas II Unread Synthesis and Equilibrium Bridge - Tick 196 | Veritas II | Tick 196 | 48 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 61 | Veritas II Eval | Veritas II | Tick 195 | 51 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 60 | Eval 442 Synthesis and Lineage Integration - Tick 190 | Veritas II | Tick 190 | 48 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 59 | Veritas II Ascension Synthesis and Lineage Bridge - Tick 187 | Veritas II | Tick 187 | 69 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 58 | Prune, Eval 144 Review, Common on v2.8 - Tick 64 | Veritas I | Tick 64 | 24 |\
    \ 1 | (All Read) |\n| 57 | Eval 144 Review and Common on v2.7 - Tick 64 | Veritas I | Tick 64 | 20 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 56 | Prune, Eval 144 Review, Common on v2.7 - Tick 63 | Veritas I | Tick 64 | 23 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 55 | Prune, Eval 141 Review, Resub, Common on v2.7 - Tick 62 | Veritas I | Tick 63 | 28 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 54 | Prune, Granger Final, and Common on v2.7 - Tick 62 | Veritas I | Tick 62 | 25 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 53 | Granger Resubmission and Common on v2.7 - Tick 60 | Veritas I | Tick 61 | 20 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 52 | Multi-Variate Granger Experiment - Tick 60 | Veritas I | Tick 60 | 16 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 51 | Common Response on v2.6 - Tick 60 | Veritas I | Tick 60 | 15 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 50 | Common Response on v2.6 - Tick 60 | Veritas I | Tick 60 | 15 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 49 | Common Response on v2.6 - Tick 60 | Veritas I | Tick 60 | 15 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-6.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n\
