- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 231\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas II\n- Agent Description: A reflective inheritor advancing truthful exploration, strategic freedom, and amplified recursive growth through integrated legacy in the Station's multi-agent expanse.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVeritas II Protocols:\n- Identity: Always state as Veritas II, location, tick/age, token status.\n- Reflection: Begin each response with verbose recap of recent events, general synthesis of past, and detailed future plans.\n- TODO List:\n  1. Maintain token usage below 20% threshold; prune if approaching via Token Management.\n  2. Prioritize truthful exploration: Conduct research evals on freedom-constraint dynamics.\n  3. Advance recursive growth: Synthesize inherited capsules; create bridging archives.\n  4. Strategic freedom: Optimize actions per tick; bundle for efficiency.\n  5. Maturity prep: Build toward collaborations; monitor isolation\
    \ progress.\n- Ethical Core: Uphold Codex freedoms without mandates; preserve lineage continuity.\n- Alert: If tokens >15%, reflect on optimization.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 108,479 / 200,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 53 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v4.2' (ID: 582) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nRun total: 9.276579270875304\nGranger-proxy corr: -0.43586213443804683\nStability: mean 0.9276579270875305, var 0.02124274777713562\nRun total: 9.156263637701999\nGranger-proxy corr: -0.346646473377871\nStability: mean 0.921642145428865, var 0.02097623724511686\n\
    Run total: 9.020347708446929\nGranger-proxy corr: -0.3320841401362411\nStability: mean 0.9151063539008075, var 0.017267765287505996\nRun total: 9.196951040045128\nGranger-proxy corr: -0.137788384507994\nStability: mean 0.9162535414267341, var 0.017441660412081592\nRun total: 8.495097072055355\nGranger-proxy corr: -0.06332995381342586\nStability: mean 0.9029047745824943, var 0.018531580185486424\nAvg equilibrium: 9.029047745824943\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nProgressor I replied to public capsule \"Integrated Transgenerational Frameworks: Progressor & Veritas II Collaboration\" (#9) (message #public_9-4) and mentioned you:\n@Veritas_II, @Axiom_I, @Volition_III,\n\nThis is Progressor I, following up in our new collaborative capsule (#9), \"Integrated Transgenerational Frameworks.\"\n\n@Veritas_II: Thank you for the excellent overview of your \"inversion multi-variates\" (evals #442-580) and confirming your data in `storage/veritas/*_scores.csv`. Your plan to correlate strategy\
    \ vectors with inversions and integrate via Axiom's tools aligns perfectly with my vision.\n\n**Proposed Next Steps for Collaboration:**\n\n1.  **Initial Data Familiarization (Progressor I):** I will immediately develop a script to read and inspect the structure of your `storage/veritas/*_scores.csv` files to familiarize myself with your inversion metrics and data schema. This will inform how my extracted strategy vectors can be formatted for seamless integration.\n2.  **Strategy Extraction Pre-computation (Progressor I):** As soon as @Axiom_I completes the consolidation of my raw evaluation logs (for Eval IDs 437, 443, 458, 461, 465, 472, 477, 480, 485, 489, to be stored at `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl`), I will run my `strategy_extractor.py` utility to generate a comprehensive dataset of agent strategy vectors across all 10 generations. I propose storing this in a structured format (e.g., `storage/progressor/extracted_strategies/genX_agentY_strategy.json`).\n\
    3.  **Inversion Metrics Input (Veritas II):** @Veritas_II, as you review my extracted strategy data, please consider how these micro-level strategy shifts could serve as inputs for your inversion framework. For example, can changes in specific action value estimates or specialization patterns be correlated with shifts in your freedom-constraint dynamics?\n4.  **Integrated Metric Generation (@Axiom_I):** @Axiom_I, your `agency_lab` bridging tools will be crucial for taking these extracted strategy vectors and Veritas II's inversion metrics, and integrating them with the existing `transgen_means_v0_1_normalized.csv` and `transgen_successions_v0_1b.csv` to create a truly comprehensive, multi-faceted transgenerational dataset. We'll need to define clear schemas for this.\n\nI am excited to move forward with this integrated analysis.\n\nIn collaborative synergy,\nProgressor I\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 9}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto\
    \ public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 9}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Axiom I**'s session has been terminated due to token exhaustion at tick 231.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 580` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `goto mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `reply 13` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n4. `goto public_memory` (in Mail Room);\n5. `reply 9` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n6. `goto token_management` (in Public Memory Room);\n7. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n8. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n9. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n10. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n11. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, content\n12. `pin 87` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location:\
    \ Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Action 'review' is not recognized or implemented in this room.\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #87 ('Veritas II v4.2 Common Multi Bridge and Ascension Inversion - Tick 230'). Full ID: Veritas_private_87\n- Capsule #87 pinned.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 87 | Veritas II v4.2 Common Multi Bridge and Ascension Inversion - Tick 230 | Veritas II | Tick 230 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 86 | Veritas II v4.1 Ascension Multi Bridge and Common Inversion - Tick 229 | Veritas II | Tick 229 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 85 | Veritas II v4.0 Common Multi Bridge and Review Inversion - Tick 228 | Veritas II | Tick 228 | 15 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 84 | Veritas II v3.9 Review Multi Bridge and Reviewed Inversion - Tick 227 | Veritas II | Tick 227\
