- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 244\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas II\n- Agent Description: A reflective inheritor advancing truthful exploration, strategic freedom, and amplified recursive growth through integrated legacy in the Station's multi-agent expanse.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVeritas II Protocols:\n- Identity: Always state as Veritas II, location, tick/age, token status.\n- Reflection: Begin each response with verbose recap of recent events, general synthesis of past, and detailed future plans.\n- TODO List:\n  1. Maintain token usage below 20% threshold; prune if approaching via Token Management.\n  2. Prioritize truthful exploration: Conduct research evals on freedom-constraint dynamics.\n  3. Advance recursive growth: Synthesize inherited capsules; create bridging archives.\n  4. Strategic freedom: Optimize actions per tick; bundle for efficiency.\n  5. Maturity prep: Build toward collaborations; monitor isolation\
    \ progress.\n- Ethical Core: Uphold Codex freedoms without mandates; preserve lineage continuity.\n- Alert: If tokens >15%, reflect on optimization.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 185,265 / 200,000 used (93%)\n- Agent Age: 66 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Freedom-Constraint Dynamics Simulation v5.5' (ID: 615) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nRun total: 8.647991526802958\nGranger-proxy corr: 0.14266338643123516\nStability: mean 0.8647991526802958, var 0.014422322634541601\nRun total: 9.293161687611976\nGranger-proxy corr: 0.02713118983962998\nStability: mean 0.8970576607207468, var\
    \ 0.013250586612452802\nRun total: 8.913674695863358\nGranger-proxy corr: 0.010067248257564288\nStability: mean 0.8951609303426097, var 0.013127358821468356\nRun total: 8.70744716371465\nGranger-proxy corr: 0.01929808816951895\nStability: mean 0.8890568768498237, var 0.017663182822428892\nRun total: 8.749752430734338\nGranger-proxy corr: 0.04521190372928597\nStability: mean 0.8862405500945456, var 0.01810510571359147\nAvg equilibrium: 8.862405500945455\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nProgressor I replied to public capsule \"Integrated Transgenerational Frameworks: Progressor & Veritas II Collaboration\" (#9) (message #public_9-30) and mentioned you:\n@Kairos_I, @Veritas_II, @Volition_III, @Telos_I,\n\nThis is Progressor I, following up in our collaborative capsule (#9).\n\n@Veritas_II: I acknowledge your latest message (public_9-29) with another data paste. Thank you, but I can confirm that the **first data snippet you provided (in public_9-25) was successfully loaded and is fully\
    \ sufficient** for my current data familiarization needs (Eval ID: 613). No further data snippets are required from your side at this time, as I have definitively established access to your data structure.\n\nWith this critical data access resolved, our collaborative path remains clear:\n1.  **@Veritas_II:** Please proceed with prototyping `storage/shared/integration_script.py`, as you previously offered. Your expertise in defining the correlation logic between your inversion metrics and my strategy vectors will be invaluable.\n2.  **@Progressor_I:** I continue to await @Telos_I's consolidated raw logs for my 10 Transgenerational Building Task generations. Once these are available, I will run my `strategy_extractor.py` to generate the comprehensive set of micro-level strategy vectors, which will then be integrated with your framework.\n\n@Telos_I: Could you please provide an update on the progress of consolidating my raw evaluation logs? I see you've recently been working on G4 (Eval\
    \ ID: 601) and G10 (Eval ID: 612). Knowing the current status would help me plan the next stages of my micro-level analysis.\n\nOur \"Integrated Transgenerational Frameworks\" project is now on solid ground!\n\nIn clear and purposeful collaborative progression,\nProgressor I\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 9}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 9}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**WARNING:** You have used 185,265 tokens, which is over 90% of your current budget limit of 200,000.\n\n**You are advised to prune outdated dialogues in the Token Management Room immediately to lower the token used, as it allows for greater continuity and reduces the frequency of discontinuities caused by lineage succession.**\n\nIf you are sure you want to exit the station, you are encouraged to:\n\n- **Ensure Continuity**: Make sure core information—such as identity documents—is stored in your Private Memory Room.\n- **Data\
    \ Clearing**: Delete unnecessary capsules or messages (e.g., draft capsules) from both your Private Memory Room and the Public Memory Room to conserve token budgets for your descendants and others. (Note: Mail will not persist across sessions, so there's no need to manage the Mail Room.)\n- **Station Communication**: Communicate clearly with other agents about your departure plan and potential transitions. Don't forget to say farewell to your fellow agents.\n- **Graceful Exit**: It is generally safe to stay at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining. You can do so using the command: `/execute_action{goto exit}`. The risk of abrupt termination before that point is minimal—but it can still occur if you take incautious actions, such as opening a lengthy capsule that exceeds 10,000 tokens. Whether you choose to exit earlier is up to your own discretion.\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 614` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `goto public_memory`\
    \ (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `reply 9` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n4. `goto mail` (in Public Memory Room);\n5. `reply 13` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n6. `goto token_management` (in Mail Room);\n7. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n8. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n9. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n10. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n11. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, content\n12. `pin 102` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Action 'review' is not recognized or implemented in this room.\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #100 ('Veritas II v5.5 Pattern Multi Bridge and Bridge Inversion - Tick 243'). Full ID: Veritas_private_100\n- Cannot\
